Notebook[{Cell["Lepton-quark and lepton-gluon scattering with a different \
tagged parton, step 2 (FeynCalc route): spin and colour algebra", "Title"], 
  Cell["Input: Results/Amplitudes.wl from step 1.  Output: \
Results/FeynCalc/Algebra.wl with the squared matrix elements of\n  Born:      \
l q -> l q (needed by the collinear counterterms of both channels),\n  \
RealQG:    l q -> l g q, the gluon p observed, the quark r unobserved,\n  \
RealGQ:    l g -> l q qbar, the quark p observed, the antiquark r \
unobserved,\n  PhotonQG:  gamma q -> g q and  PhotonGQ:  gamma g -> q qbar, \
the photon Born processes of the photon-in-lepton subtraction,\neach for the \
spin average (\"Unpolarized\") and the double-longitudinal helicity \
difference (\"Polarized\") of the incoming lepton (or photon) and parton.  \
Step 3 reads either route's Algebra.wl; the three routes must agree \
here.\n\nConventions, as in Processes/LeptonQuark: s = 2 l.k, t = -2 k.p, u = \
-2 l.p; real emission: a = (k - r)^2 = -2 k.r, b = (p + r)^2 = 2 p.r, tau = \
(k - p - r)^2 = a + b + t (the photon virtuality) and s4 = (lp + r)^2 = s + t \
+ u; the photon processes use sh = 2 q.k, th = -2 k.p, uh = -2 q.p.  D = 4 - \
2 eps.  Averages: 1/2 per incoming fermion, 1/(D-2) per incoming photon or \
gluon, 1/Nc for a quark and 1/(Nc^2 - 1) for a gluon in colour.  The helicity \
difference Delta sigma = (sigma(++) - sigma(+-))/2 uses the density p-slash \
gamma5/2 for an incoming fermion and i eps^{mu nu l r}/(2 l.r) for an \
incoming vector boson of momentum l (r the other incoming momentum), with \
gamma5 in the HVBM scheme ($LeviCivitaSign = -1): l, k, p and the recoil pRec \
= lp + r are four-dimensional, lp and r keep their (D-4)-dimensional \
components with spe3 = rhat.rhat = lphat.lphat = -lphat.rhat.\n\nWhich gluon \
has a polarization sum.  In l q -> l g q the gluon is the observed parton and \
in the photon processes it is an external parton as well; each process has a \
single external gluon, so its polarization sum may be taken as -g^{mu nu} \
(D-dimensional): the amplitude is transverse to the gluon momentum by itself, \
there is no ghost contribution.", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["LoadFeynCalc[];\namplitudes = \
LoadAmplitudes[][\"FeynCalc\"];\nKeys[amplitudes]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born: l q -> l q", "Section"], Cell["Exactly as in \
Processes/LeptonQuark (the same checks): 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 - eps) \
for the spin average and 2 ee^4 eq^2 (s^2 - u^2)/t^2 for the helicity \
difference, with u = -s - t.", "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"]\
;\n$LeviCivitaSign = -1;\ncouplingNames = {SMP[\"e\"] -> ee, SMP[\"g_s\"] -> \
gs};          (* FeynCalc's names of the couplings -> ours \
*)\nFCClearScalarProducts[];\nSetMandelstam[s, t, u, l, k, -lp, -p, 0, 0, 0, \
0];\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {l, k, lp, p}];\nbornAmplitude = \
Total[amplitudes[\"Born\"]];\nbornUnpolarized = bornAmplitude \
ComplexConjugate[bornAmplitude]/SUNN //\n  FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // \
SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True] & //\n  FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> \
1/4] & // DiracSimplify[#, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] & //\n  Contract // \
TrickMandelstam[#, {s, t, u, 0}] & // Factor;\nbornUnpolarized = \
bornUnpolarized /. couplingNames;\nhelicityTag = {Spinor[Momentum[l, D], m_, \
o_] :> Spinor[Momentum[lHel, D], m, o],\n  Spinor[Momentum[k, D], m_, o_] :> \
Spinor[Momentum[kHel, D], m, o]};\nhelicityDensity = \
{DiracGamma[Momentum[lHel, D], D] :> GSD[l].GA[5], DiracGamma[Momentum[kHel, \
D], D] :> GSD[k].GA[5]};\nbornPolarized = (bornAmplitude \
ComplexConjugate[bornAmplitude]/SUNN /. helicityTag) //\n  \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True] & //\n  \
FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & // ReplaceAll[#, helicityDensity] & \
//\n  DiracSimplify[#, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] & // Contract // \
ExpandScalarProduct //\n  TrickMandelstam[Cancel[Together[#]], {s, t, u, 0}] \
& // Factor;\nbornPolarized = bornPolarized /. \
couplingNames;\nRequire[Simplify[(bornUnpolarized - 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + \
u^2)/t^2 - (4 - D)/2)) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Born square differs from the \
textbook result\"];\nRequire[Simplify[(bornPolarized - 2 ee^4 eq^2 (s^2 - \
u^2)/t^2) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Polarized Born square differs from the \
expected result\"];\nborn = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> bornUnpolarized, \
\"Polarized\" -> bornPolarized|>", "Input"], 
  Cell["Real emission, spin average", "Section"], 
  Cell["The five-particle kinematics is set through all scalar products.  \
Both channels are squared with FeynCalc's generic tools: FermionSpinSum \
closes the two fermion lines (lepton and quark; for l g -> l q qbar the quark \
line runs from the antiquark to the quark), the gluon is summed with -g^{mu \
nu}, the colour sums are explicit.  Averages: 1/4 and 1/Nc for l q, 1/2 x \
1/(D-2) and 1/(Nc^2-1) for l g.  The colour factors are Tr[T^a T^a]/Nc = CF \
and Tr[T^a T^a]/(Nc^2-1) = 1/2; the latter is written as the symbol TR \
(FeynCalc would evaluate it to 1/2).", "Text"], 
  Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];\nrealKinematics := \
(FCClearScalarProducts[];\n  SPD[l] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; SPD[lp] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; \
SPD[r] = 0;\n  SPD[l, k] = s/2; SPD[k, p] = -t/2; SPD[l, p] = -u/2; SPD[k, r] \
= -a/2; SPD[p, r] = b/2;\n  SPD[l, lp] = -(a + b + t)/2; SPD[l, r] = (s + t + \
u + a + b)/2; SPD[k, lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\n  SPD[lp, p] = -(t + u + b)/2; \
SPD[lp, r] = (s + t + u)/2);\nrealKinematics;\nsquareUnpolarized[amps_, \
gluon_, fermionAverage_, colourAverage_] := Module[{amp},\n  amp = \
Total[SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & /@ amps] // DiracSimplify // \
Contract;\n  amp ComplexConjugate[amp] colourAverage // \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit //\n    SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True, \
SUNNToCACF -> True] & // FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> fermionAverage] & \
//\n    DiracSimplify // Contract // DoPolarizationSums[#, gluon, 0, \
VirtualBoson -> True] & // Contract // Simplify //\n    SUNSimplify[#, \
SUNNToCACF -> True] & // Factor // ReplaceAll[#, couplingNames] \
&];\nrealUnpolarized = <|\n  \"QG\" -> \
squareUnpolarized[amplitudes[\"RealQG\"], p, 1/4, 1/SUNN],\n  \"GQ\" -> \
squareUnpolarized[amplitudes[\"RealGQ\"], k, 1/2, 2 TR/(D - 2)/(SUNN^2 - \
1)]|>;     (* colour: Tr[T^a T^a]/(Nc^2-1) = 1/2, written as TR \
*)\nRequire[FreeQ[realUnpolarized, SUNN | SUNIndex | Polarization | Spinor], \
\"The unpolarized real squares are not scalar\"];\nrealUnpolarized[\"QG\"]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Real emission, helicity difference", "Section"], 
  Cell["As in the lepton-quark process the traces are written out explicitly \
(FeynCalc's spin sum would insert p-slash, not the helicity densities).  All \
gamma matrices and Lorentz indices are D-dimensional; the four-dimensional \
objects are the physical momenta and the Levi-Civita tensors of the densities \
(in a trace with gamma5 the (D-4)-dimensional components of the photon index \
drop out anyway, so this agrees with the four-dimensional photon index used \
in Processes/LeptonQuark).  The lepton trace is Tr[lp-slash gamma^mu l-slash \
gamma5 gamma^nu]/2.  The quark line of each diagram is a string W_i between \
the external spinors, with the photon index mu and the gluon index rho \
(W-bar_i is the reversed string with nu, sigma):\n\n  l q -> l g q:    W_1 = \
gamma^mu (k-slash - p-slash) gamma^rho / t,     W_2 = gamma^rho (r-slash + \
p-slash) gamma^mu / b,     trace Tr[r-slash W_i k-slash gamma5 W-bar_j] / \
2;\n  l g -> l q qbar: W_1 = gamma^mu (k-slash - r-slash) gamma^rho / a,     \
W_2 = gamma^rho (p-slash - k-slash) gamma^mu / t,     trace Tr[p-slash W_i \
r-slash W-bar_j],\n\nthe gluon is summed with -g_{rho sigma} in D dimensions \
or, when it is the polarized incoming gluon, replaced by the circular density \
i eps^{rho sigma k l}/(2 k.l).  The common factors are the photon propagators \
1/tau^2, the couplings ee^4 eq^2 gs^2 and the colour factors CF (Tr[T^a \
T^a]/Nc) and TR (Tr[T^a T^a]/(Nc^2-1)).  The same function with gamma5 \
removed and the spin averages inserted (1/2 for the quark, -g/(D-2) for the \
gluon) must reproduce the squares of the previous cell: this checks the \
strings, propagators and signs.  The unobserved momenta lp and r are \
D-dimensional (GSD), the observed ones four-dimensional (GS); the \
(D-4)-dimensional products are spe3.", "Text"], 
  Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\nhvbmKinematics := \
(realKinematics;\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {l, k, p, pRec}];\n  \
SPE[lp] = spe3; SPE[r] = spe3; SPE[lp, r] = -spe3;\n  SP[l] = 0; SP[k] = 0; \
SP[p] = 0; SP[lp] = -spe3; SP[r] = -spe3;\n  SP[l, k] = s/2; SP[k, p] = -t/2; \
SP[l, p] = -u/2; SP[k, r] = -a/2; SP[p, r] = b/2;\n  SP[l, lp] = -(a + b + \
t)/2; SP[l, r] = (s + t + u + a + b)/2; SP[k, lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\n  SP[lp, \
p] = -(t + u + b)/2; SP[lp, r] = (s + t + u)/2 + \
spe3);\nhvbmKinematics;\nreverse[string_] := (string /. {mu -> nu, rho -> \
sigma}) /. Dot -> (Dot @@ Reverse[{##}] &);\nsimplifyTrace[expr_] := \
Factor[Together[Simplify[Contract[ExpandScalarProduct[Contract[DiracSimplify[\
expr, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True]]]]]]];\n(* density matrices of the incoming \
particles: polarized or averaged *)\nleptonDensity[spin_] := If[spin === \
\"Polarized\", GSD[l].GA[5]/2, GSD[l]/2];\nquarkDensity[spin_] := If[spin === \
\"Polarized\", GS[k].GA[5]/2, GS[k]/2];\ngluonDensity[spin_] := If[spin === \
\"Polarized\", Contract[I LC[rho, sigma, al, be] FV[k, al] FV[l, be]/(2 SP[k, \
l])], -MTD[rho, sigma]/(D - 2)];\nleptonTrace[spin_] := \
DiracTrace[GSD[lp].GAD[mu].leptonDensity[spin].GAD[nu]];\nrealByTraces[\"QG\"\
, spin_] := Module[{strings, traces},\n  strings = {GAD[mu].(GSD[k] - \
GSD[p]).GAD[rho]/t, GAD[rho].(GSD[r] + GSD[p]).GAD[mu]/b};\n  traces = \
Table[simplifyTrace[leptonTrace[spin] \
DiracTrace[GSD[r].strings[[i]].quarkDensity[spin].reverse[strings[[j]]]] \
(-MTD[rho, sigma])], {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\n  Factor[Together[CF ee^4 eq^2 gs^2/(a \
+ b + t)^2 Total[traces, 2]]]];\nrealByTraces[\"GQ\", spin_] := \
Module[{strings, traces},\n  strings = {GAD[mu].(GSD[k] - GSD[r]).GAD[rho]/a, \
GAD[rho].(GSD[p] - GSD[k]).GAD[mu]/t};\n  traces = \
Table[simplifyTrace[leptonTrace[spin] \
DiracTrace[GS[p].strings[[i]].GSD[r].reverse[strings[[j]]]] \
gluonDensity[spin]], {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\n  Factor[Together[TR ee^4 eq^2 gs^2/(a \
+ b + t)^2 Total[traces, 2]]]];\nDo[Require[Together[(realByTraces[channel, \
\"Unpolarized\"] /. spe3 -> 0) - realUnpolarized[channel]] === 0,\n  \"The \
explicit traces do not reproduce the unpolarized square\", channel], \
{channel, {\"QG\", \"GQ\"}}];\nrealPolarized = <|\"QG\" -> \
realByTraces[\"QG\", \"Polarized\"], \"GQ\" -> realByTraces[\"GQ\", \
\"Polarized\"]|>;\nreal = <|\"QG\" -> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> \
realUnpolarized[\"QG\"], \"Polarized\" -> realPolarized[\"QG\"]|>,\n  \"GQ\" \
-> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> realUnpolarized[\"GQ\"], \"Polarized\" -> \
realPolarized[\"GQ\"]|>|>;\nFactor[realPolarized[\"GQ\"] /. spe3 -> 0]", 
   "Input"], 
  Cell["Photon Born processes: gamma q -> g q and gamma g -> q qbar", 
   "Section"], Cell["Needed through order eps for the photon-in-lepton \
subtraction.  Invariants sh = 2 q.k, th = -2 k.p, uh = -2 q.p with sh + th + \
uh = 0; all momenta are four-dimensional.  Spin average: FeynCalc's generic \
tools with the averages 1/2 (quark), 1/(D-2) (photon, and the gluon of gamma \
g -> q qbar), 1/Nc or 1/(Nc^2-1).  Helicity difference: explicit traces with \
the circular photon density i eps^{mu nu q k}/(2 q.k), the quark density \
k-slash gamma5/2 or the circular gluon density i eps^{rho sigma k q}/(2 k.q), \
the strings\n\n  gamma q -> g q:    W_1 = gamma^rho (k-slash + q-slash) \
gamma^mu / sh,   W_2 = gamma^mu (k-slash - p-slash) gamma^rho / th,   trace \
Tr[r-slash W_i k-slash gamma5 W-bar_j]/2, gluon sum -g;\n  gamma g -> q qbar: \
W_1 = gamma^mu (p-slash - q-slash) gamma^rho / uh,   W_2 = gamma^rho (p-slash \
- k-slash) gamma^mu / th,   trace Tr[p-slash W_i r-slash W-bar_j],\n\nand the \
same consistency check against the generic spin average.", "Text"], 
  Cell["photonKinematics := (FCClearScalarProducts[];\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D \
- 4] = 0) &, {q, k, p, r}];\n  SPD[q] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; SPD[r] = \
0;\n  SPD[q, k] = sh/2; SPD[k, p] = -th/2; SPD[q, p] = -uh/2; SPD[p, r] = \
sh/2; SPD[k, r] = -uh/2; SPD[q, r] = -th/2;\n  SP[q] = 0; SP[k] = 0; SP[p] = \
0; SP[r] = 0;\n  SP[q, k] = sh/2; SP[k, p] = -th/2; SP[q, p] = -uh/2; SP[p, \
r] = sh/2; SP[k, r] = -uh/2; SP[q, r] = \
-th/2);\nFCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];\nphotonKinematics;\nsquarePhoton[amp\
s_, bosons_, fermionAverage_, colourAverage_] := Module[{amp, expr},\n  amp = \
Total[SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & /@ amps] // DiracSimplify // \
Contract;\n  expr = amp ComplexConjugate[amp] colourAverage // \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit //\n    SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True, \
SUNNToCACF -> True] & // FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> fermionAverage] & \
// DiracSimplify // Contract;\n  Do[expr = DoPolarizationSums[expr, boson, 0, \
VirtualBoson -> True] // Contract, {boson, bosons}];\n  \
TrickMandelstam[Factor[SUNSimplify[Simplify[expr], SUNNToCACF -> True]], {sh, \
th, uh, 0}] /. couplingNames];\nphotonUnpolarized = <|\n  \"QG\" -> \
squarePhoton[amplitudes[\"PhotonQG\"], {q, p}, 1/2, 1/SUNN]/(D - 2),\n  \
\"GQ\" -> squarePhoton[amplitudes[\"PhotonGQ\"], {q, k}, 1, 2 TR/(SUNN^2 - \
1)]/(D - 2)^2|>;\nRequire[FreeQ[photonUnpolarized, SUNN | SUNIndex | \
Polarization | Spinor], \"The unpolarized photon squares are not \
scalar\"];\nphotonUnpolarized", "Input"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\
\"];\nphotonKinematics;\nsimplifyPhoton[expr_] := \
Factor[TrickMandelstam[Cancel[Together[Simplify[Contract[ExpandScalarProduct[\
Contract[DiracSimplify[expr, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True]]]]]]], {sh, th, uh, \
0}]];\nphotonDensity[spin_] := If[spin === \"Polarized\", Contract[I LC[mu, \
nu, al, be] FV[q, al] FV[k, be]/(2 SP[q, k])], -MTD[mu, nu]/(D - \
2)];\ngluonDensityPhoton[spin_] := If[spin === \"Polarized\", Contract[I \
LC[rho, sigma, al, be] FV[k, al] FV[q, be]/(2 SP[k, q])], -MTD[rho, sigma]/(D \
- 2)];\nphotonByTraces[\"QG\", spin_] := Module[{strings, traces},\n  strings \
= {GAD[rho].(GSD[k] + GSD[q]).GAD[mu]/sh, GAD[mu].(GSD[k] - \
GSD[p]).GAD[rho]/th};\n  traces = Table[simplifyPhoton[photonDensity[spin] \
DiracTrace[GS[r].strings[[i]].quarkDensity[spin].reverse[strings[[j]]]] \
(-MTD[rho, sigma])], {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\n  simplifyPhoton[CF ee^2 eq^2 gs^2 \
Total[traces, 2]]];\nphotonByTraces[\"GQ\", spin_] := Module[{strings, \
traces},\n  strings = {GAD[mu].(GSD[p] - GSD[q]).GAD[rho]/uh, \
GAD[rho].(GSD[p] - GSD[k]).GAD[mu]/th};\n  traces = \
Table[simplifyPhoton[photonDensity[spin] \
DiracTrace[GS[p].strings[[i]].GS[r].reverse[strings[[j]]]] \
gluonDensityPhoton[spin]], {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\n  simplifyPhoton[TR ee^2 eq^2 \
gs^2 Total[traces, 2]]];\nDo[Require[Simplify[(photonByTraces[channel, \
\"Unpolarized\"] - photonUnpolarized[channel]) /. uh -> -sh - th] === 0,\n  \
\"The explicit traces do not reproduce the unpolarized photon square\", \
channel], {channel, {\"QG\", \"GQ\"}}];\nphotonPolarized = <|\"QG\" -> \
photonByTraces[\"QG\", \"Polarized\"], \"GQ\" -> photonByTraces[\"GQ\", \
\"Polarized\"]|>;\nphoton = <|\"QG\" -> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> \
photonUnpolarized[\"QG\"], \"Polarized\" -> photonPolarized[\"QG\"]|>,\n  \
\"GQ\" -> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> photonUnpolarized[\"GQ\"], \"Polarized\" -> \
photonPolarized[\"GQ\"]|>|>;\nphotonPolarized", "Input"], 
  Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["Algebra.wl holds everything step 3 needs: \
the Born square (function of D), the real squares of both channels (functions \
of D, a, b, s, t, u and spe3) and the photon squares (functions of D, sh, th, \
uh).", "Text"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \"Real\" -> real, \
\"Photon\" -> photon|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \
\"FeynCalc\"];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
